Job Description

As Senior IT Business Analyst – CRM, you play a key role in shaping Fugro’s global CRM landscape and revenue operations capability. You bring clarity, structure and business insight to a complex, multi-region transformation, ensuring the future CRM platform delivers harmonised processes, improved forecast accuracy and measurable business value.

Acting as the link between senior stakeholders across Sales, Operations, Finance and IT, you translate business needs into a global CRM blueprint and execution roadmap. Working closely with Business Process Owners and Technology Portfolio Managers, you drive a standardised global CRM platform, allowing local configurations only where justified.

Based in Nootdorp, this value-driven role sits at the heart of connecting business, IT and transformation. While Microsoft Dynamics 365 is a key strategic programme, the role also covers the broader Customer Relationship domain, including sales solutions and related systems. You will lead business analysis for a global Dynamics 365 transformation across Fugro’s Marine and Land business lines, helping shape a future-fit CRM environment.

Your role

You lead change management, training and adoption, and act as a role model and mentor for the wider Business Analyst team while advising C-level and senior stakeholders.
You act as trusted advisor to senior business stakeholders, Business Process Owners and senior technical stakeholders  you own the business analysis agenda, guide executive decision-making on scope and priorities, and align Sales, Operations, Finance and IT around one harmonised global direction;
You own current-state analysis and requirements gathering  supporting the mapping of end-to-end revenue lifecycles for business lines, CRM-versus-ERP ownership, handoffs and pain points, capturing regional variations;
You validate the proposed KPI framework and assess forecasting methodology and forecast accuracy across regions and business areas;
You guide the production and quality-assure the core deliverables  D365 sales evaluation report, current-state architecture, revenue lifecycle and customer journey maps, Business Requirement Document (BRD), fit/gap analysis and solution blueprint;
You translate the blueprint into build-ready functional specifications and user stories for a single global D365 CE / Dataverse platform, clearly distinguishing global-standard capabilities from local configuration;
You help shape and maintain the global CRM template, common data model and localization approach, managing a controlled backlog of region- and business-area-specific variations to prevent unnecessary customization;
You specify integrations to regional and downstream ERP/finance systems, addressing multi-currency, multi-language, time-zone and data-residency requirements;
You plan and support a phased rollout  build, data migration, integration, testing/UAT with key users and deployment;

Your track record

You have a bachelor’s or master’s degree in IT, Computer Science, Business Administration or a related field;
You have 7+ years of business analysis experience, including CRM transformation and at least one full-lifecycle, multi-region Dynamics 365 (Customer Engagement / Sales) implementation across multiple business units;
You have strong knowledge of D365 CE (Sales), Dataverse modelling and global-template design in a multi-region context, plus revenue-lifecycle, order-to-cash and revenue-leakage/margin-variance analysis;
You are experienced in producing BRDs, fit/gap analyses, user stories and test cases, and are familiar with Power Platform/Power BI, integration patterns and basic SQL for validating KPIs;
You are proactive and self-managing, and a strong communicator able to be the central point of contact for senior stakeholders across regions and both business areas;
Microsoft Dynamics 365 / Power Platform certifications are strongly preferred; ITIL/ITSM and data-analysis certifications are a plus. English – fluent; additional languages an advantage.

What Fugro Offers

A competitive gross monthly salary in line with the seniority of the role, with opportunities for growth;
29 holidays per year based on fulltime employment (of which 4 are appointed by Fugro management) and the possibility to purchase 12 additional days;
Extensive career & training opportunities both nationally and internationally;
Flexible working hours and the ability to work from home 2 days a week in accordance with your manager and corporate policies;
Commuting allowance, a modern pension scheme and collective health insurance;
Possibility to register with our corporate fitness plan and coaching options through our EAP (Employee Assistance Program).

Are you interested?

Please visit our Company Page to find out more on what it is like to work at Fugro.

If you have any further questions, please contact Umit Nesar, Corporate Recruiter, tel. +31 (0)6 – 81 41 07 68.

After you have applied

You will receive an automated confirmation email of the receipt of your application;
When we see a match, we will invite you for the first interview within a couple of days. Of course, you will also receive a message if we will not invite you;
After a successful first round, you will be invited for the second round;
If we are both still positive after the second interview, we will make you an offer and with that we hope to welcome you at Fugro!

Disclaimer For Recruitment Agencies

Fugro does not accept any unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies. Acquisition to Fugro Recruitment or any Fugro employee is not appreciated.

Help shape the future of maritime innovation.

About PortXL

PortXL is the world’s first port & maritime accelerator, founded in 2015 and based in Rotterdam. We bridge the gap between ambitious start-ups and scale-ups and the established maritime industry, working alongside corporate partners, investors and ecosystem leaders to make maritime climate-positive. We search, match and accelerate the newest technologies from around the world. Our home is the Innovation Dock at RDM Campus: an inspiring hub where shipbuilding history meets the future of shipping, energy, logistics and ports.

What You’ll Be Doing

As our AI & Operations intern, you will work at the intersection of emerging technology and organisational excellence. You will help PortXL leverage AI tools to scale its scouting, matching and communication workflows while also keeping the daily operations of a fast-moving accelerator running smoothly. One of the real challenges of this role is finding smart, creative ways to optimise processes and implement AI with only limited financial resources available. Resourcefulness and a hands-on mindset are essential.

- Explore, test and implement AI tools that improve how PortXL scouts start-ups, manages data and communicates with its network;

- Help automate repetitive workflows using tools such as Make, Zapier, Notion AI, Airtable or similar platforms;

- Identify creative, low-cost solutions to operational challenges — getting maximum impact from minimal tooling;

- Analyse and improve internal processes to boost efficiency across the team;

- Support the development of data pipelines or dashboards that provide operational insight;

- Document and standardise processes so that knowledge is captured and easily shared;

- Work on ad hoc operational and innovation projects alongside the PortXL team;

- Stay on top of developments in applied AI, particularly relevant to the maritime and innovation sector.

We Offer

- An energetic, mission-driven team with a shared ambition to transform the maritime industry;

- Access to an international network of start-ups, scale-ups and maritime innovators;

- Involvement with our corporate partners, including the Port of Rotterdam, City of Rotterdam and the Ministry of Defense;

- Room to discover your interests, think creatively and take real ownership;

- An inspiring workspace at the Innovation Dock, RDM Campus, Rotterdam;

- Opportunities to attend maritime events, demo days and ecosystem gatherings;

- Personal and professional development;

- Compensation: €575 per month based on 36 hours per week. Part-time is possible with a minimum of 24 hours per week; our preference is 32–36 hours. A minimum of 3 days per week from the office;

- Duration: minimum 5 months, with a preference for 6–7 months.

What You Bring

- Currently enrolled in the later phases of your Bachelor’s or Master’s degree, for example in Business Informatics, Computer Science, Innovation Management, AI or a related field;

- More important than your exact field of study: you have a hands-on drive to build and improve — you love experimenting with AI tools, automating the tedious and making systems work smarter with limited means;

- Structured thinker who can translate complex processes into clear, workable systems;

- Experience with tools like Notion, Airtable, Make, Zapier, Python or similar is a strong plus;

- Comfortable working resourcefully — you know how to deliver results without a big budget;

- Entrepreneurial mindset: proactive, solutions-oriented and comfortable with ambiguity;

- Good written and spoken English.

Are you a software engineer with a passion for hands-on creativity, ready to make your mark in a groundbreaking R&D environment? Look no further – at Allseas R&D, located in the vibrant tech hub of Eindhoven, we are on the lookout for a talented individual to join our multidisciplinary team.

At Allseas R&D Eindhoven, we are not just pioneers; we are disruptors in the field of offshore inspection technologies. As an integral part of Allseas Engineering, we combine the financial stability of a major industry player with the agility and innovation of a small, startup-inspired team. Our Eindhoven office serves as the hub for cutting-edge R&D, focusing on crafting specialized equipment tailored for the challenges of the offshore environment.

Your role

As a Software Engineer, you will play a pivotal role in our dynamic development team, contributing to the full development cycle of inspection systems and robotics applications. We are not just seeking a coder – we're looking for a creative thinker who is unafraid to dive into hardware challenges and add fresh insights to our innovative projects. Your hands-on approach will be integral to shaping the future of offshore technology.

What You Will Do

Address complex problems within a unique and challenging environment;
Be a key player in a multidisciplinary team working on robotic pipe crawlers, ultrasonic weld inspection equipment, automated weld systems, and digitalization initiatives;
Embrace the freedom to innovate, learn, and explore, from proof-of-concept to production.

What we expect from you

Software Engineering degree or equivalent;
Solid knowledge of object-oriented development principles;
Eagerness to learn, try, fail, and explore;
Team player with a broad interest in technology;
Proficiency in C# 10.0/12.0 and the .NET 8.0 (beneficial).

What we Offer

You will contribute to cutting-edge projects at the forefront of offshore technology. Be part of a small, agile team with creative freedom and multidisciplinary collaboration. Thrive in a culture that values hands-on innovation and a commitment to quality.

You Can Expect

Competitive industry benchmarked salary and excellent pension;
Performance based salary raises and bonuses;
30 holidays days per year, flexible working hours;
Extensive training and development programme, study budgets and coaching;
A close-knit community, BBQ’s, parties and Friday afternoon drinks.

Allseas has earned the "World-class Workplace" label. This means that as an employer we score above Effectory's global benchmark for being a good employer. The label is based solely on feedback from our employees. Wondering what our people say about working at Allseas? Read their stories.

Interested?

If you feel that you can contribute to our business by diving into this exciting opportunity, we are looking forward to receiving your CV and motivational letter!

Please apply via the ‘Apply’ button.

An online personality questionnaire can be part of the selection procedure.

Acquisition is not appreciated.
